This is a third-party binary package, not an official Debian/Ubuntu archive entry.
The frontend needs a separately installed makemkvcon engine on PATH to process
media. No engine package name is assumed and no proprietary engine is bundled.
The upstream frontend is MIT licensed; the engine has its own requirements.

The package is classified contrib/video because media processing requires the
separately licensed external engine. This binary repackaging recipe is not a
Debian archive-quality source package. Official archive submission additionally
needs Debian source packaging, dependencies, sponsorship and policy review.

State lives in the user's XDG/HOME state directory; this package creates no
system state, services, privileged users or configuration. Removing the package
does not remove batch plans, preferences, staged data or completed outputs.
